    "created_at": "2020-02-23T18:35:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-02-23T18:35:28Z",
    "body": "> Starship overrides any prompt configuration defined by Oh My Zsh.\r\n\r\nI don't think that's true. If the user disables Oh My Zsh theme and enables Starship, then it'll work fine. But if they get an Oh My Zsh theme and Starship enabled at the same time, then two bad things may happen.\r\n\r\n1. Prompt might be slower than it should be (both themes get evaluated).\r\n2. Prompt from Oh My Zsh visible and not the Starship prompt. You can also get left prompt from Starship and right prompt from Oh My Zsh.\r\n\r\nFor example, try installing Oh My Zsh and enabling `trapd00r` theme. Then enable Starship. You'll get (1) for sure. Depending on the order of config lines you might see either Starship or trapd00r in prompt.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
